  "question": {
    "text": "The magnetic moment of a bar magnet is $0.5 \\mathrm{Am}^2$. It is suspended in a uniform magnetic field of $8 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~T}$. The work done in rotating it from its most stable to most unstable position is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KrJyy",
      "text": "$8 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Ftij4",
      "text": "$4 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8guON",
      "text": "Zero",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oYUA4",
      "text": "$16 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At stable equilibrium\n$\\mathrm{U}=-\\mathrm{mB} \\cos 0^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{mB}$<br />At unstable equilibrium\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{U}=-\\mathrm{mB} \\cos 180^{\\circ}=+\\mathrm{mB} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{W}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U} \\\\\n& \\text { W.D. }=2 \\mathrm{mB} \\\\\n& =2(0.5) 8 \\times 10^{-2}=8 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~J}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
